{"bullets":["The oceans cover more than 70% of the Earth's surface and are vital for regulating climate and supporting life.","They contain the majority of the Earth's water and play a crucial role in weather patterns and ocean currents.","Oceans are home to a vast diversity of marine life, from microscopic organisms to the largest animals on Earth.","They serve as a major source of food, transportation, and economic activity for millions of people worldwide.","Oceans face increasing threats from pollution, overfishing, and climate change, highlighting the need for conservation and sustainable practices."],"status":"written","title":"Oceans"}